{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "NTiedtkeDeepDepartureScan",
    "description": "The DEEP phase of `cutypen`, the convection trigger of WRF's New Tiedtke scheme (`phys/physics_mmm/cu_ntiedtke.F90:1517-1748`, WRF 4.8): a departure-level SCAN. After the shallow test parcel (shallow_ascent.esm), cutypen launches a second test parcel from each half level in turn, from klev-2 upward to klev/2+1 (28 departures on 59 levels), skipping departures more than 350 hPa above the surface, and ACCEPTS the first (lowest) whose parcel rises into a cloud at least 200 hPa deep. An accepted departure makes the column penetrative (`ktype = 1`), overriding the shallow verdict, and the scan stops.\n\nONE DEPARTURE. The parcel at departure level L leaves half level L+1 with the environment's dry static energy and humidity there -- or, within 60 hPa of the surface, with their pressure-weighted means over a mixed layer of up to three half levels (L+2, L+1, L, added while the layer is under 50 hPa) -- plus fixed excesses of 0.2 K and 1e-4 kg/kg, and kinetic energy 0.5 m^2/s^2. From there it rises exactly as the shallow parcel does, with the step shared through parcel_templates.esm (entrain by the EarthSciDiscretizations plume stencil, condense by cuadjtqn's kcall = 1 adjustment, refreeze, re-form, load, compare, advance the kinetic energy, locate the base), with three differences: the entrainment rate is 1.75e-3 times min(1, (q_sat[k]/q_sat[L])^3) rather than the shallow parcel's 0.8/z + 2e-4; the running condensate is HALVED at every level rather than capped; and the first step mixes the parcel against the departure air's own dry static energy at L+1 (the Fortran overwrites dhen(L+1) with it) but against the half-level humidity pqenh(L+1), which it does not overwrite.\n\nTHE SCAN IS A REDUCTION, NOT A LOOP. Every departure's ascent is independent of every other's; the only coupling is \"stop at the first success\". So the component computes all 28 ascents side by side on a (dep, lev) grid, judges each as if it were tried (`deep_if_tried`), and then marks a departure TRIED when it is inside the window and no lower departure in the window would have succeeded (`n_deep_below` = 0). The departures above the accepted one, which the Fortran never runs, are carried as zeros, as the tape records them.\n\nWHY EACH ASCENT IS FORCED FROM THE TAPE: the parcel's (s, q) is a recurrence over two distinct variables through the saturation adjustment, which esm-spec 4.3.1.1 does not admit (EarthSciAST #701, which proposes the recurrence group that would). The full argument is in shallow_ascent.esm's description; it applies unchanged. Each departure's levels are therefore stepped from that departure's TAPED state one level down (`T_tr`, `q_tr`, `dh_tr`: the dp_* tape, one column per departure), and every operation of the step is pinned; the condensate and the kinetic energy are genuine single-variable recurrences along `climb` with `dep` as a non-recurrence axis. A float64 reimplementation that closes the loop instead reproduces the same tape over all 16 steps x 2 tile columns x 28 departures with every departure's base, top, acceptance and tried flag identical, and the arrays to 5e-15 (T, q, dh) and 1.3e-12 (condensate, kinetic energy, buoyancy) of their maxima.\n\nCUTYPEN'S VERDICT IS PROVISIONAL, TWICE (measured on the chem170 reference, WRF fork commit cf3a2bdf, which tapes cutypen's own outputs as ty_*). The shallow verdict is overridden by this scan: at step 1730 the tape's one shallow cloud becomes deep (ty_ktype 1). And THIS verdict is overridden in turn after cutypen returns: the scheme's final ktype differs from cutypen's at 7 of the 16 steps -- 918, 1080, 1621, 2400 and 2521 end as mid-level convection (3, set later by cubasmcn, for columns cutypen called inactive), at 2134 column 1 likewise, and at 689 and 2134 column 2 the column cutypen called DEEP ends as SHALLOW (2) -- cumastrn reclassifies a deep cloud whose updraught (cuascn) proves too shallow. So `ktype` here is cutypen's output, not the scheme's, and a coupling must not read it as the convection type; the final type belongs to the components for cuascn, cubasmcn and the closure.\n\nThe tie to the shallow phase -- its verdict, base, top and cloud-base velocity -- comes in as four scalars (`*_shallow`) so that `ktype`, `cubot`, `cutop`, `kdpl` and `wbase` are cutypen's complete outputs; a mounting document supplies them from shallow_ascent.esm. The routine's copy of the accepted parcel into cutu/cuqu/culu/culab is not exposed: cuascn recomputes those arrays.\n\nConstants: the seven cu_ntiedtke_init arguments from lib/wrf_constants.esm at binary64; the scan's literals (0.2, 1e-4, 60e2, 50e2, 350e2, 1.75e-3, 0.5) in ntiedtke_parameters.esm at their binary32 roundings (FORTRAN_BUGS N109). The cloud-base comparison reads the condensation pressure truncated to whole pascals, as the Fortran stores it in an integer (FORTRAN_BUGS N114).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "wrf",
      "cumulus",
      "ntiedtke",
      "cutypen",
      "trigger"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Number of model layers in the scheme's top-down ordering (the kernel's klev); 59 is the chem170 single-column reference."
    },
    "NDEP": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 28,
      "description": "Number of departure levels the scan can try, (NLEV - 2) - (NLEV/2 + 1) + 1 with Fortran integer division -- 28 for NLEV = 59. A metaparameter of its own because esm-spec 9.7.6 folds `/` only when it divides exactly; bind it with NLEV."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NLEV"
    },
    "lev_nodes": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          "NLEV",
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "climb": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NLEV"
    },
    "dep": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NDEP"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "NTiedtkeDeepDepartureScan": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./parcel_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
        },
        "par": {
          "ref": "./ntiedtke_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "phi": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer geopotential pgeo (kernel top-down ordering)."
        },
        "qs": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Environmental saturation mixing ratio of each layer, pqsen: it sets how fast the deep parcel entrains."
        },
        "T_h": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Environmental temperature at half level k, ptenh."
        },
        "q_h": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Environmental mixing ratio at half level k, pqenh."
        },
        "phi_h": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Geopotential of the NLEV+1 half levels, pgeoh."
        },
        "p_h": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Pressure of the NLEV+1 half levels, paph."
        },
        "T_tr": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "TEACHER TRAJECTORY, one column per departure: the parcel temperature each departure's ascent carries out of each level, as taped (dp_ptu). Read only one level below the level being stepped (EarthSciAST #701; see the description)."
        },
        "q_tr": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "TEACHER TRAJECTORY: the parcel mixing ratio carried out of each level, per departure (dp_pqu)."
        },
        "dh_tr": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "J/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "TEACHER TRAJECTORY: the parcel dry static energy carried out of each level, per departure (dp_dh)."
        },
        "ktype_shallow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The shallow phase's verdict (shallow_ascent.esm `ktype`: 2 or 0), which the deep scan overrides only if it accepts a departure."
        },
        "kcbot_shallow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The shallow phase's cloud-base level (shallow_ascent.esm `kcbot`)."
        },
        "kctop_shallow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The shallow phase's cloud-top level (shallow_ascent.esm `kctop`)."
        },
        "wbase_shallow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "The shallow phase's cloud-base velocity (shallow_ascent.esm `wbase`)."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Height of the step from half level k+1 to k, (phi_h[k] - phi_h[k+1])/g."
        },
        "s_env": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "J/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Environmental dry static energy at half level k, phi_h + cp T_h."
        },
        "Tv_env": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Environmental virtual temperature at half level k."
        },
        "k_scan_top": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Highest level the scan departs from (cutypen's itoppacel): the smallest k whose upper half level lies less than 350 hPa above the surface."
        },
        "in_scan": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "1 for a departure inside the scan's 350 hPa window (departure level >= k_scan_top)."
        },
        "mixed_launch": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "1 when the departure level lies within 60 hPa of the surface, so its parcel is taken from a pressure-weighted MIXED layer of up to three half levels rather than from the half level below the departure."
        },
        "n_mixed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "Number of half levels in the launch mixed layer: added from L+2 upward while the accumulated depth is under 50 hPa -- 1, 2 or 3."
        },
        "T_launch": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "The departure air's T_h: its pressure-weighted mean over the mixed layer when mixed_launch, else T_h at half level L+1."
        },
        "q_launch": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "The departure air's q_h: its pressure-weighted mean over the mixed layer when mixed_launch, else q_h at half level L+1."
        },
        "phi_launch": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "The departure air's phi_h: its pressure-weighted mean over the mixed layer when mixed_launch, else phi_h at half level L+1."
        },
        "s_launch": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "J/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "Dry static energy of the departure air, phi_launch + cp T_launch. It REPLACES the environment's at half level L+1 in the first entrainment step."
        },
        "dh_seed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "J/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel dry static energy at departure, s_launch + cp 0.2 K."
        },
        "q_seed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel mixing ratio at departure, q_launch + 1e-4."
        },
        "T_seed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "dep"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel temperature at departure, from dh_seed at the geopotential of half level L+1."
        },
        "eta": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Entrainment rate of departure d's parcel at level k: 1.75e-3 times min(1, (qs[k]/qs[L])^3) -- weaker where the air is colder and drier than at the departure."
        },
        "s_env_dep": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "J/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The environmental dry static energy departure d's first step mixes against: s_launch at half level L+1, s_env elsewhere. (The humidity's first step uses the half-level q_h, not q_launch: the Fortran overwrites dhen(L+1) and not pqenh(L+1).)"
        },
        "dh_c": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "J/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel dry static energy carried out of level k: the departure value at L+1, the teacher trajectory elsewhere (EarthSciAST #701)."
        },
        "q_c": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel mixing ratio carried out of level k: the departure value at L+1, the teacher trajectory elsewhere (EarthSciAST #701)."
        },
        "T_c": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel temperature carried out of level k: the departure value at L+1, the teacher trajectory elsewhere (EarthSciAST #701)."
        },
        "dh_mix": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "J/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel dry static energy after entraining from k+1 to k (`entrain_step`)."
        },
        "q_mix": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel mixing ratio after entraining (`entrain_step`): cutypen's zqold."
        },
        "T_mix": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel temperature after entraining."
        },
        "T_up": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "dep",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Parcel temperature after condensing (cuadjtqn kcall = 1, `up_adjust_T`)."
